<title>USA: Ingram Micro gets split-off OK'd, IPO starts.</title>
<headline>Ingram Micro gets split-off OK'd, IPO starts.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA ANA, Calif. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ingram Micro Inc said Friday it will proceed immediately with its initial public offering after getting approval for the split-off of Ingram Industries Inc.</p>
<p>The microcomputer company was forced to delay its IPO pending Internal Revenue Service approval for the split-off of Ingram Industries, which will include Ingram Barge Co, Ingram Materials Co, Ingram Book Group and Permanent General Cos.</p>
<p>The split-off is the first part of Ingram Micro's reorganization into three independent businesses -- Ingram Micro, Ingram Industries and Ingram Entertainment Inc, which distributes video rentals and sales.</p>
</text>
